Literature sweep completed 2026-05-04.

Source PDB and numbering convention:
- Chain A of pikp1_avrpia_complex.pdb is an AlphaFold3 monomer prediction of
  native Pikp-1 HMA (UniProt E9KPB5, residues 186–263), renumbered 1–78
  such that pipeline position 1 = Pikp-1 residue 186 and position 78 =
  Pikp-1 residue 263. Translation: pipeline = literature − 185.
- Chain B is AVR-Pia coordinates lifted from PDB 6Q76 chain B (Varden 2019
  JBC; Pikp-1 HMA / AVR-Pia complex, 1.90 Å). Chain B is deposited as
  residues 1–68 (66 modelled); the relationship to AVR-Pia precursor
  numbering (1–85, signal peptide 1–19) must be confirmed by ChimeraX
  inspection before complex assembly. Working assumption is precursor
  numbering (so chain B Arg-43 = precursor Arg-43 = the conserved
  salt-bridge partner of Pikp-1 Asp-217).
- The 6Q76 chain A numbering (1–75) coincides exactly with pipeline
  numbering (both start at Pikp-1 186). Complex assembly aligns the AF3
  chain A onto 6Q76 chain A directly — no extra cross-complex alignment
  template needed. 6G10 is not used.
- Structural-input fallback ladder rung: rung 5 for chain A (shared AF3
  monomer, same as all pikp1_* campaigns). Rung 1 for chain B (native
  target-effector complex deposited in the PDB).

Binding face determination:
- AVR-Pia binds the α1/β2 face of Pikp-HMA (the HMA dimerization face),
  NOT the canonical AVR-Pik face (Interfaces 1/2/3). Confirmed by 6Q76
  (Varden 2019) and independently by 5ZNG (Guo 2018) for the structurally
  equivalent RGA5/AVR1-CO39 interface. This face is opposite to the
  AVR-PikD binding surface.
- Primary redesign region: pipeline positions ~14–42 (α1 second half + β2).
  Contact residues: Ser-204(19), Ser-212(27), Asp-217(32), Val-219(34),
  Arg-226(41). Asp-217 (pipeline 32) is the most conserved contact across
  all AVR-Pia binding HMA domains; it is absent in Pikm-HMA (replaced by
  His), explaining why Pikm does not bind AVR-Pia.

Primary papers cited:
- Varden 2019 JBC (6Q76 structure; Pikp-HMA/AVR-Pia interface)
